cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this code or these results, please cite the repository."
title: "Endothermy buffers assemblage trait composition against environmental filtering across Chinese terrestrial vertebrates"
abstract: >-
  Code and aggregated results for a study of assemblage-level functional trait
  structure in 2,837 Chinese terrestrial vertebrates (birds, mammals, reptiles,
  amphibians) on nested 50-km and 100-km equal-area grids. The analysis uses
  families as replicates to test whether thermoregulatory mode predicts the
  strength of trait-environment coupling, decomposes assemblage trait
  distributions into their first four moments, applies fourth-corner max tests
  to avoid the Type I error inflation of naive community-weighted-mean
  regression, and evaluates conservation gaps against China's protected areas.
authors:
  - family-names: Ding
    given-names: Chenchen
    affiliation: Peking University
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0000-0000-0000"
keywords:
  - functional biogeography
  - community assembly
  - thermoregulation
  - trait-environment coupling
  - terrestrial vertebrates
  - China
  - conservation gap analysis
